{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789254294,"nonce":"/cVAzfIY6wVMeeNe6TGWjF4Ow0w=","message":"Reproduced natively on macOS arm64 after the hatch sync brought the current fsm spec in: 100% crash at default thresholds, deterministic with --jit-threshold 1. Root cause: a run loop entered through a bridge (call_closure_sync from compiled code) unwound an error without popping the frames it was raised in, so the caller's next register store went into a taken (empty) register file; also the interpreter's inline JIT call path and the constructor JIT path never consumed a callee's error, so aborts inside Fiber.try escaped to the enclosing fiber, and a krio-backed fiber whose caller was set by the JIT fiber-call path ran the caller's frame on its own stack after routing. Fixed in b7fcd7e25370b32109b334f0f7eaf1086cf6ae5d; fsm 82/82 at default thresholds and at --jit-threshold 1, and the pure-Wren package specs pass at --jit-threshold 1 --opt-threshold 4 except hatch-proc's async streaming (separate issue).","files":null}]}